  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1216 PM MDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nMoisture advection will ramp up significantly Tuesday into\nWednesday, partially attributable to moisture transport behind \nthe backdoor front and mostly because of an impressive Monsoon \nmoisture plume that is forecast to stand up over the region. The\nsqueeze play between an approaching Pacific low and the upper \nhigh along the TX coast will play out Tue/Wed in a very wet \nscenario, with continuation into Thu/Fri across eastern NM. PWATs \nare forecast to rise up and challenge calendar day records Tue/Wed\nand then settle back down to between the 90th percentile and \ncalendar day records Thu/Fri. WPC has included much of our area in\na slight risk for excessive rainfall on Tuesday and Wednesday and\nwill likely see an upgrade for Wednesday to a moderate risk for \neast central and south central portions of NM. Deeper convection \nwith higher rainfall rates are likely Tuesday on the front end of \nthe moisture advection due to greater instability, especially \nacross western NM. Widespread showers with embedded thunder are \nforecast late Tuesday night through Wednesday, so rainfall rates \nwill likely retreat due to much less instability with a rain- \ncooled lower boundary layer. The high temperature forecast for our\narea on Wednesday continues to trend down and we're lagging the \nGFS MOS, which currently shows a high of 64 degrees at the \nAlbuquerque Sunport. The Pacific low is forecast to open up and \npull northeast away from the region around the upper high \ncirculation late Wednesday into Thursday, reorienting the Monsoon \nmoisture plume to more over eastern NM where a continued heavy \nrainfall and flood threat will reside. River flooding is possible \nWed/Thu, but more likely Thursday across eastern NM as two days \nworth of rainfall runoff gradually makes it's way into the main \nstems. PWATs will trend down Friday through the weekend as the \nupper high over TX ridges westward across northern MX and shuts \nour moisture tap off. Residual moisture will be sufficient for \nmore limited daily rounds of convection Friday through Sunday, \nwhile temperatures trend back up closer to average.",
